Subject: [PATCH 012/230] Stop the dead shot-plotter route and the blank
 Expected table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

/match/:id/shot-plotter was still routed but had no page behind it, so a
stale link or an old push landed on a blank screen. Redirect it to the
predict tab that replaced it, via a component rather than <Navigate to>,
because Navigate's target is a literal string and would have baked the
":id" placeholder into the URL.

The Expected view rendered an empty grid whenever a league had no
Understat data — which is every league outside the big five, since the
Understat sync is hard-scoped to those five. Hide the view entirely when
there is nothing to show, so the Table screen never offers a tab it
cannot fill.

That made the two empty-state strings a lie ("the next sync fills this
table"), so they now say what is actually true: no expected data for
this competition.

